## Overview
End‑to‑end regression pipeline to predict house prices using the Kaggle House Prices dataset. Compares Linear Regression and Random Forest models, selecting the best performer (Random Forest) based on RMSE and R².

## Features
- 💻 Data loading and cleaning (missing value imputation, one‑hot encoding)
- 📈 Feature scaling with `StandardScaler`
- 🤌 Model comparison: Linear Regression vs Random Forest
- 🎩 Visualisations: feature importance, actual vs predicted plots, model comparison table
- 💻 Ready-to‑use Jupyter notebook (`house_price_prediction.ipynb`)

## How to Run
```bash
cd 29-Machine-Learning-HousePrice
pip install -r requirements.txt
python train_model.py
```
Or launch the notebook:
```bash
jupyter notebook house_price_prediction.ipynb
```
